.TH smi-forward "1" "October 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-forward \- Switch the nftables redirect of 80 and 443 between nginx and HAProxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-forward
.BR nginx | haproxy
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-forward
points ports 80 and 443 at one of the two web fronts:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nginx      80 -> 8080    443 -> 8081
haproxy    80 -> 8090    443 -> 8091
.fi
.RE
.PP
The
.B web_proxy
chain of the
.B inet global_firewall
table holds nothing but a jump to the chain of the front that is on duty, and this command
replaces that jump, in one
.B nft
transaction:
.PP
.RS
.nf
flush chain inet global_firewall web_proxy; add rule inet global_firewall web_proxy jump to_nginx
.fi
.RE
.PP
The ports are not in this command.
They are in the
.B to_nginx
and
.B to_haproxy
chains of the ruleset, which redirect 80 and 443 to the port pair of their front, so a port is
defined once, in the ruleset, and changing one needs no change here.
.PP
Because the chain is flushed first, the jump to the other front is gone by definition and the
command can be run again and again with the same result.
The chain is reached from
.B pre_nat
for arriving traffic and from
.B out_nat
for traffic of the machine itself, so both follow the switch; nothing else of the ruleset is
touched.
.PP
It has to be run as root and needs the ruleset loaded, because it changes a chain of a table that
has to exist already.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B nginx
Jump to the
.B to_nginx
chain, which redirects to 8080 and 8081.
.TP
.B haproxy
Jump to the
.B to_haproxy
chain, which redirects to 8090 and 8091.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The chain now jumps to the chosen web front.
.TP
.B 1
Wrong or missing argument.
.TP
.I other
Exit status of
.BR nft (8),
for example when the table or one of the chains does not exist, or the command is not run as
root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Serve the sites straight from nginx:
.RS
.nf
sudo smi-forward nginx
.fi
.RE
.PP
Put HAProxy in front, for example to give draft previews their cookie check:
.RS
.nf
sudo smi-forward haproxy
.fi
.RE
.PP
What is redirected now:
.RS
.nf
sudo nft list chain inet global_firewall web_proxy
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
.PP
The change is made in the running ruleset only.
The stored configuration keeps whatever its
.B web_proxy
chain says, which is
.B jump to_nginx
in the shipped
.IR /etc/nftables/main.nft ,
so a reload or a reboot goes back to nginx.
Change that one line as well when a front has to stay after a restart.
.PP
The table name and the three chain names are fixed in the command, matching that ruleset. The
front ports live there too, as
.BR PORT_NGINX_HTTP ", " PORT_NGINX_HTTPS ", " PORT_HAPROXY_HTTP
and
.BR PORT_HAPROXY_HTTPS ;
nginx listens on 8080 and 8081, HAProxy on 8090 and 8091, and neither needs a privileged port of
its own.
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
